for n,v in json.loads((R/'inputs/preflight-design-manifest.json').read_text())['members'].items():assert digest(R/'inputs'/n)==v
f=json.loads((R/'lossless-fixture-results.json').read_text());s=json.loads((R/'static-and-raw-results.json').read_text())
assert f['case_count']==26 and s['raw_case_count']==10 and all(c['result']=='PASS' for c in f['cases']+s['cases'])
result={'decision':'ACCEPT','scope':'FINAL_PREFLIGHT_DESIGN_AND_ISOLATED_LOCAL_COMPONENTS_ONLY','helper_sha256':H,'design_manifest_sha256':M,'proposed_scope':scope,'findings':[],'local_component_case_count':26,'local_byte_case_count':10,'total_local_cases':36,'original_block_reports_immutable':True,'walk_fail_closed':True,'ancestor_and_entry_symlinks_rejected':True,'partial_payload_bytes_opened':False,'nonzero_partial_count_requires_separate_custody_before_startup':True,'bounded_handoff_seconds':180,'late_io_acceptance_rejected_and_response_retained':True,'timeout_original_bytes_roundtrip':True,'coherent_worker_timer_attempts_and_races_retained':True,'pin_definition_only_and_lock_compatible':True,'outer_module_and_unaffected_metadata_bindings_unchanged':True,'allowed_next_step':'After parent full hash/size readback, one actual metadata-only preflight using these exact bytes; inspect and independently bind its actual result before subsequent qualification or startup.','not_accepted':['actual current handoff','actual partial-zero census','genuine affected Linux qualification','admission or ARM','new capture or T0','elapsed duration or historical time transfer','saved-frame audit or capacity','source stability or CPU/network cause'], 'helper_main_or_whole_remote_executed':False,'real_subprocess_network_or_service_called':False,'production_source_or_data_modified':False,'raw_manifest_or_partial_payload_opened':False,'new_remote_scope_created':False,'formal_credit_seconds':0,'linux_credit':False}
(R/'RESULT.json').write_text(json.dumps(result,sort_keys=True,indent=2)+'\n')
(R/'REPORT.md').write_text('''# Lossless stopped preflight successor — ACCEPT

This decision binds helper `abe667eca3ced0666dd4e2f54a9335218ca93b6f5cb512e01308300249ef8ef6` and design manifest `cd8f711e837878612148d97151fb113e2df43c4590aecf51bb4c99a16fb59148` for the still-proposed scope `/srv/recorder-data/recorder-archive/evidence/R2-capacity-n2-readiness-retry-20261025-1s0kswlt`. The original d103 and intermediate 4f4c BLOCK reports remain immutable; neither was remotely executed. This is design and isolated LOCAL component acceptance only.

All five previously reported defects are addressed. Directory scan errors fail closed; trusted directory ancestors and entries reject symlinks, missing entries and nonregular files. Nonzero retained partials remain metadata only and set the startup custody gate false. The whole worker/journal/inventory/owner/timer/final-worker attempt is bounded by one 180-second monotonic deadline, with remaining-time subprocess/D-Bus timeouts and post-I/O checks. A changed worker invocation or expired timer observation triggers a bounded retry with attempts retained. The contract correctly describes the definition-only canonical VERIFY.

The final successor also preserves failure evidence before rejecting it. Timed command responses are attached to their attempt before post-I/O deadline assertions. Commands use byte capture; stdout/stderr retain base64, byte count and SHA, with strict UTF-8 decoding as an additional view. Invalid UTF-8 parsed state is rejected. Timeout original bytes are retained both with the command attempt and in the exception envelope, without replacement decoding. In-progress inventory and file metadata are attached before the next deadline check.

Twenty-six isolated LOCAL handoff cases pass: coherent success, nonzero-partial gating, scan/ancestor/directory/file/FIFO rejection, late successful state and journal responses, invalid-byte state/journal timeouts, bounded busy worker, worker and timer races, changed Recorder, failed or malformed worker, masked owners, disabled timer, journal errors, invalid UTF-8 state/stderr and inventory expiration. Ten additional byte cases verify None/empty/binary/Unicode encodings, exact CRLF byte retention, strict decode errors and invalid state rejection. The two former custody failures now round-trip exact original bytes while still rejecting the failed/late operation. Static comparisons confirm unchanged outer module AST, read-only preflight bindings outside the reviewed command/handoff corrections, unchanged final metadata result AST, and exact source/identity/config/failed-attempt creation window and canonical pin argv.

The pin uses only LoadUnit/RefUnit/UnrefUnit around the installed canonical `deployment verify` command as bmdr. It does not start Recorder. Prior static source inspection confirmed that deployment verification does not acquire the runtime service lock; the exclusive stopped preflight lock is compatible. The helper performs no remote scope creation, capture, restoration, start/stop/disable/mask/reboot action or Raw/manifest/partial payload read. The current census uses readonly SQLite metadata, and current CPU context is diagnostic.

After full parent hash/size readback, the exact design may be used for one actual metadata-only preflight. Its real output still needs independent binding. An enabled natural archive timer is not frozen: the returned worker/timer proof describes its bounded observation interval and finite future monotonic deadline at collection, not a permanent inactive guarantee. A nonzero partial inventory requires a separate reviewed custody action before startup. Genuine affected Linux qualification, current reserves/admission, fresh bindings/window and a new own86400 start remain future work. This review supplies zero Linux, duration, saved-data, capacity, stability-repair or CPU/network causal credit; all failed data, old time and closed guards remain unchanged.
''')
